WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:07.027
From late 1991,
Stepanakert lay under siege.

2
00:00:07.067 --> 00:00:10.597
Azerbaijani forces held Shushi
on the heights above,

3
00:00:10.637 --> 00:00:13.814
and from there
they fired on the city below.

4
00:00:14.174 --> 00:00:17.664
The chief weapon was the BM-21 Grad,

5
00:00:17.704 --> 00:00:22.281
a truck-mounted launcher that throws
a ripple of forty rockets at once.

6
00:00:22.321 --> 00:00:24.791
Rockets struck houses, schools,

7
00:00:24.831 --> 00:00:27.463
the silk factory
and the maternity hospital.

8
00:00:27.503 --> 00:00:32.453
Families moved into basements, and
the city lived by candle and radio.

9
00:00:32.813 --> 00:00:36.923
The war had grown from
the Karabakh movement of 1988,

10
00:00:36.963 --> 00:00:40.073
and every side lost civilians.

11
00:00:40.433 --> 00:00:43.463
On the night of 8 May 1992,

12
00:00:43.503 --> 00:00:46.863
Armenian units under
Arkady Ter-Tadevosyan

13
00:00:46.903 --> 00:00:50.122
attacked Shushi
up the cliffs and roads.

14
00:00:50.162 --> 00:00:52.132
By 9 May the town was taken,

15
00:00:52.172 --> 00:00:55.305
and the bombardment
of Stepanakert ended.

16
00:00:55.665 --> 00:00:59.634
Keep the basements safe
until the heights are won.

